# Build output
/bin/
# `go build ./cmd/...` drops the binary in the repo root
/arblab

# Go test/coverage artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# NOTE: testdata/fuzz/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Go keeps its generated
# corpus in $GOCACHE/fuzz; it writes into testdata/fuzz/ only when it finds a
# FAILING input, and those are regression cases we want committed.

# rapid writes a fail file next to the test whenever a property fails. Unlike a
# fuzz corpus entry these are not a durable regression suite — they are keyed to
# a rapid version and an internal bit stream, and they go stale. A real find
# belongs in the hand-written table as a named case, so the fail file is a
# working artifact only.
#
# The leading **/ is load-bearing and was missing until 2026-07-29. A gitignore
# pattern containing a mid-string slash is ANCHORED TO THE REPO ROOT, so plain
# `testdata/rapid/` matched only a top-level directory that has never existed —
# the rule read as enforced and excluded nothing, and ids' five fail files had
# been tracked since the day the rule was written. `git check-ignore -v <path>`
# is how to check that a rule here actually fires.
**/testdata/rapid/

# The live capture archive (configs/capture.json roots it at ./archive).
# Unrecoverable-by-construction data, never source: tracking it would put an
# ever-growing binary tree in git status, and an accidental commit of a partial
# hour would create a second, diverging copy of a file whose whole value is
# being the only honest one.
/archive/

# The §42b screening raw store: hundreds of megabytes of venue REST
# responses, verbatim. Re-derivable from the venues (settled funding is
# backfillable — the §42a asymmetry), and every file's sha256 is pinned
# in the COMMITTED research/screening/ledger.json, so a divergent
# refetch is visible. Committing the bytes would buy nothing the ledger
# doesn't already prove.
/research/screening/raw/

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor-only workspace file. Deliberately NOT committed: a go.work would let
# the root module resolve golang.org/x/tools through tools/lint, silently
# defeating the reason tools/lint is a separate module.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Stray tooling artifact
logger.log
/capture.log
/screening-run.log
